      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "reference_info",
      "content": "## Common Pressure Units Reference\n\n**Key Notes:**\n- 1 Torr = 1 mm Hg\n- Pressure is \"force per unit area\"\n- Units like kg/cm² are technically mass units; mass must be multiplied by gravity g to be a force (weight)\n\n### Example: Convert 10 psi to Pa\nFrom the conversion table, 1 psi = 6894.76 Pa:\n- 10 psi × 6894.76 = 68,947.6 Pa = 68.95 kPa\n\n### Additional Pressure Units\n- 1 Pa = 0.00001 Bar\n- 1 Pa = 0.0000102 Atmosphere (metric)\n- 1 Pa = 0.000145 Pound force/square inch\n- 1 Pa = 0.0000093 Standard atmosphere\n- 1 Pa = 1 Newton/square meter"
